== Trivia ==
* This effect is the same as {{c|Tainted Isaac}}'s passive 'more options' effect. 
** It's also identical to the {{i|Birthright}} effect for [[Isaac]].
** This Soul Stone, along with {{p|Soul of Magdalene}}, {{p|Soul of Judas}}, and {{p|Soul of Samson}}, replicates a feature of the character it's unlocked by.

== Bugs ==
{{bug|If an active item on a pedestal is touched and then rerolled with {{p|Soul of Isaac}}, the alternate item will also count as "already picked up": it will not drop pickups, grant health or transformations like it  normally would.}}

